    [echo/structure concern] The sentence follows the same two-beat structure as the Bartimaeus episode: blind man by the road cries out, crowd rebukes him to be silent — even the ordering and causal link mirror the verse.
    [echo/scene concern] The scene (blind man beside the road, crowd's rebuke) is the same specific episode rather than a generic setting freshly imagined.
    [reasoning unsound] The reasoning defends the swap test for κράζω's semantic class but never notices that the second clause is not original composition — it is Mark 10:48's wording lightly re-inflected. The reasoning treats the sentence as freshly built when it is substantially borrowed.

